<component type="console-application">
  <id>io.github.dzobash.apptrol</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>

  <name>Apptrol</name>
  <summary>Control each app's volume with a hardware MIDI controller</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.dzobash">
    <name>Dzobash</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Apptrol turns a Korg nanoKONTROL2 into a volume mixer for PipeWire: every
      slider and knob controls one app or microphone, so the desktop's mixer is no
      longer needed for everyday volume changes.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Volume, mute and solo per app, with the controller's LEDs showing the state</li>
      <li>Microphone buttons: mute, hold to talk, cough, and turning music down while you talk</li>
      <li>Media keys and play or pause per app, through MPRIS</li>
      <li>Buttons that start apps or commands</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Apptrol runs in the background as a systemd user service and has no window: it is
      set up in one configuration file. Enable it once with
      systemctl --user enable --now apptrol.
    </p>
  </description>

